{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The quick-setting epoxy felt useful for small repairs alongside my recent screws and anchors, because it offers another way to secure or mend something.",
    "The three-roll duct tape pack fits temporary holding and patching during repair work, with a quantity I could reasonably use."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The wire connectors, plumbing fitting, and inspection camera require specific projects I have not shown a need for; doing repair work does not mean I need every kind of repair supply.",
    "The washers need a matching fastener size and purpose, while the polishing compounds serve a task unrelated to my recent fastening purchases.",
    "Medicine cups do not imply that I use a TENS device, and twelve rolls of duct tape exceed my current needs even though a smaller pack appeals to me."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat tools and maintenance supplies as interchangeable, when their actual uses determine whether I would choose them.",
    "A single purchase of medicine cups seems to have been stretched into an interest in unrelated medical supplies."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of nails, wood screws, and drywall anchors point most clearly toward fastening and mounting work.",
    "Exact dimensions and compatibility matter for specialized hardware; a broadly related item is not useful without a matching task.",
    "Quantity matters: I would choose a manageable tape pack for current repairs without wanting a much larger supply."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my repair needs but extended them too broadly into specialized supplies without a clear use in my current work."
}"}
